{"name":"Jet Ski","hex":"#5492af","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jet ski","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small motorized watercraft with a flattish hull and an upright centre, which a rider sits astride."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To ride on a jet ski."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jet_ski"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jet ski","blocks":[{"text":"A personal watercraft (PWC)—often referred to as a jet ski or jetski, after the product line by Kawasaki, or water scooter—comically referred to as a boater-cycle, is a primarily recreational watercraft that is designed to carry a small number of occupants, who sit or stand on top of the craft, not within the craft as in a boat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Couple_of_teenagers_riding_a_jetski_splashing_on_the_Mekong_in_Laos.jpg/330px-Couple_of_teenagers_riding_a_jetski_splashing_on_the_Mekong_in_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet_ski","wikidata":"Q5175316"},{"title":"Jet Ski (brand)","blocks":[{"text":"Jet Ski is the brand name of a personal watercraft (PWC) manufactured by Kawasaki, a Japanese company. The term Jet ski is often used generically to refer to any type of personal watercraft used mainly for recreation, and it is also used as a verb to describe the use of any type of PWC. It mainly competed against Yamaha's WaveRunner, BRP's Sea-Doo, Elaqua's E-PWC and Honda's AquaTrax."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Jetboot_Jetski_DM_2007_Krautsand_2.jpg/330px-Jetboot_Jetski_DM_2007_Krautsand_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jet_Ski_(brand)","wikidata":"Q5175704"},{"title":"Ski","blocks":[{"text":"Skis are runners that are designed to glide over snow. Skiers employ them in pairs, attached to ski boots with ski bindings, with either a free, lockable, or partially secured heel. For climbing slopes, ski skins can be affixed at the base of each ski to prevent them from sliding backwards. Originally used as a means of travel over snow, skis have become specialized for recreational and competitive alpine and cross-country skiing. Skis may also be attached to vehicles, such as aircraft or snowmobiles."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ski","wikidata":"Q172226"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Couple_of_teenagers_riding_a_jetski_splashing_on_the_Mekong_in_Laos.jpg/500px-Couple_of_teenagers_riding_a_jetski_splashing_on_the_Mekong_in_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Couple_of_teenagers_riding_a_jetski_splashing_on_the_Mekong_in_Laos.jpg/1280px-Couple_of_teenagers_riding_a_jetski_splashing_on_the_Mekong_in_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Couple_of_teenagers_riding_a_jetski_splashing_on_the_Mekong_in_Laos.jpg/500px-Couple_of_teenagers_riding_a_jetski_splashing_on_the_Mekong_in_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A watercraft on the Mekong River","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACouple_of_teenagers_riding_a_jestski_splashing_on_the_Mekong_in_Laos.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/2021_RecDeck_Platform_01.jpg/500px-2021_RecDeck_Platform_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/2021_RecDeck_Platform_01.jpg/1280px-2021_RecDeck_Platform_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/2021_RecDeck_Platform_01.jpg/500px-2021_RecDeck_Platform_01.